 candidate for governor for his party  the nationalist party  and there are two parties of boys state  federalists and nationalists and stephen  this unlikely underdog  is been selected by his party to be  their candidate's voice in the storm  [Music]  stephen  and he's about it's we're entering the  kind of climactic  final vote to see if he'll be elected  governor and this scene is  really a chance to for steven to talk  about his politics his campaign  how he's chosen to conduct himself at  boys state which is very different than  some of the other boys we meet  in the film and um he takes us down to  the texas state capitol which is an  extraordinary building and he  he takes us through the legislative  chamber where you see all the boys have  taken over passing bills first about  banning prius drivers and sort of jokey  things but then actually now they're  debating really serious stuff  like uh passing uh background check  bills and  things that really matter in people's  lives so it's a chance for us to follow  stephen into this space  but i've had to listen to people who  have said things that i vehemently  opposed and disagreed with  we agree that we do need to work to  identify illegal immigrants  for their own safety it's not just for  the safety of the nation but i listen  with an open mind  so i propose a law to where law  enforcement can still use drones out of  their line of sight  there are a lot of people that i've met  that have different lives than i have  their upbringing what issues affect them  next thing we know  there were gunshots and everything it  happened in the art hallway  so can feel carry i feel is here to stay  because  in my hometown rolling oak small was  shot up but  someone with a concealed carry license  was able to fight back people don't like  the word compromise  but there's so many things that we've  been able to come together  background checks this is nonpartisan we  are simply making sure  that guns do not fall into the hands of  those who will use them to harm other  people  so um you used that moment uh  uh to to create this great uh shot  uh tell us you know what inspired you  guys  uh to to film it the way that you did  the main event was um was make or break  right if we did not capture something in  that moment the lightning in the bottle  if it did not exist we would not have a  film and i think that kind of pressure  um was was new to us but also kind of  wonderful i mean it was a new challenge  and we really had to hold on tight and  it was very risky i think that what  is so powerful to me is sort of  stephen's initial um idea there  in the campaign is what he used  throughout that entire week  um which couldn't have been easy right  stephen i mean you definitely had to  listen to a lot of  politics you don't agree with yeah it  was um  thinking about it right now that i i  follow a lot of conservative media not  because i agree with it but because it  challenges me to see why is it that why  do you believe  what you believe the way i wanted to run  my campaign  was very different from most i wanted to  know what was on your minds and ask you  what issues matter to you  i didn't want to run a campaign i did  not want to run a campaign  to represent y'all if i didn't know who  was going to represent i didn't know  y'all want y'all to sign  a bad check with my petition so i'm  really proud of the 30 signatures  that i got admittedly it is not easy it  is very difficult to kind of bite your  tongue and  you know uh sometimes it gets the better  of me where it's just like you're  absolutely 100  wrong um you know but you just kind of  step back and realize that  a message of unity won an election  flip georgia got 80 million votes and  it's kind of getting to know  what issues are affecting you that maybe  we're ignoring or that we're not  thinking about the right way or that  brief  you know haven't addressed properly to  make you vote in the way that you did  as a person who's you know part of a  partisan political party  [Music]  well stephen um i am putting my faith in  you  to figure this all out and amanda and  jesse thank you for making this movie  very provocative i hope everyone sees it  and uh  we're gonna wrap this up thank you all  thanks ann  thank you anne  [Music]  you

